{
  "id": "grammar.a1.79.a",
  "title": "Months of the year",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "hónap means 'month'. Hungarian month names are close to their international counterparts and, like the days of the week, are written lowercase."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "január – december",
      "rows": [
        [
          "január",
          "January"
        ],
        [
          "február",
          "February"
        ],
        [
          "március",
          "March"
        ],
        [
          "április",
          "April"
        ],
        [
          "május",
          "May"
        ],
        [
          "június",
          "June"
        ],
        [
          "július",
          "July"
        ],
        [
          "augusztus",
          "August"
        ],
        [
          "szeptember",
          "September"
        ],
        [
          "október",
          "October"
        ],
        [
          "november",
          "November"
        ],
        [
          "december",
          "December"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "content": "Say the months out loud — január, február, március — and you'll hear how close they already are to their Latin-rooted cousins in English."
    }
  ]
